@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "auto.provisioning"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Zendesk Account Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account information transfers properly to zendesk in the form of a ticket.

Setup:
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | zen.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | zen.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | ZEN                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | zen.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | zen.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | ZEN                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |

Teardown:
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                   |
	| DXP Non-Production               |
	| Portal Production                |
	| DXP Development                  |
	| Commerce Subscription Production |
	| DXP Unlimited Enterprise-Wide    |
	| LXC SM Subscription              |
	| Analytics Cloud Subscription     |
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENKORKORZEN  |
	| ZENKORKORZEN1 |
	| ZENKOR        |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| ZENKORKORZEN  |
	| ZENKORKORZEN1 |
	| ZENKOR        |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| zen.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| zen.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| zen.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| zen.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| zen.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}     |
	| New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}     |
	| New Subscription(s) for Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName}     |
	| Renewal Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Korzen - ${staticProjectName}                             |
	| Korzen - ${staticProjectName}                             |
	| Korzen - ${staticProjectName}                             |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| zen.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| zen.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View new business ticket
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to create a new business in Dossiera and viewing the project in the form of a zendesk ticket

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | zen.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | ZEN                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | zen.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | ZEN                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korzen - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	#Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync to be more reliable. Analise if can be taken out once the account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should be synced to zendesk
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the subject "New Business: New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the text "Account Name: Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the text "Account Code: ZENKORKORZEN" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the text "Opportunity Type: New Business" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the text "New DXP Production (1)" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the text "New Platinum Subscription" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the text "Start Date - End Date: ${staticStartYear}" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the text "US Provisioning - Working with 2019 H2 Pricing Promotions: Grow Link" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the requester with the email address "provisioningrequest@liferay.com"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the organization "Provisioning"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the product "prd_provisioning_request"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the provisioning component "opportunity_invoiced"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the support region "provisioning_united_states"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the opportunity owner "zen.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the email cc "zen.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" should have the primary address country "United States"

Scenario: View existing business ticket
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to create an existing business in Dossiera and viewing the project in the form of a zendesk ticket

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | ZENKOR                        | |
	| Name   | Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T4                            | |
	And I create a child account for an account with the name "Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | ZENKORKORZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Korzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T4                            | |
	And I create an external link for the account "Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
