Scenario: View existing business ticket with notes
	Testing the ability to create an existing business with pinned notes in Dossiera and viewing the project in the form of a zendesk ticket

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | ZENKOR                        | |
	| Name   | Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T4                            | |
	And I create a child account for an account with the name "Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | ZENKORKORZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Korzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T4                            | |
	And I create an external link for the account "Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Zenkor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                       |
	And I create a note for the account "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Content  | Account Note1 Content |
	| Format   | HTML                  |
	| Priority | 1                     |
	| Status   | Approved              |
	| Type     | General               |
	And I create a note for the account "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Content  | Account Note2 Content |
	| Format   | Plain                 |
	| Priority | 1                     |
	| Status   | Approved              |
	| Type     | General               |
	And I create a note for the account "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Content  | Account Note3 Content |
	| Format   | HTML                  |
	| Priority | 2                     |
	| Status   | Approved              |
	| Type     | General               |
	And I create a note for the account "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Content  | Account Note4 Content |
	| Format   | Plain                 |
	| Priority | 2                     |
	| Status   | Approved              |
	| Type     | General               |
	And I create a note for the account "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Content  | Account Note5 Content |
	| Format   | HTML                  |
	| Priority | 1                     |
	| Status   | Archived              |
	| Type     | General               |
	And I create a note for the account "Korzen - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Content  | Account Note6 Content |
	| Format   | Plain                 |
	| Priority | 1                     |
	| Status   | Archived              |
	| Type     | General               |
